# Names only. The real file is /etc/bulig/worker.env (root, mode 0600), written by `set-secret.sh --worker-env`, read by bulig-worker.service.
# The worker refuses to start without at least one --repo.
# One --repo <kernelPath>=<localClone> per repository the worker may work on. The kernel's path is where the kernel keeps that repo;
# the clone is the worker's own copy, made by the worker's user (bulig-cli.sh --as worker --exec git clone <url> <path>).
#
#   BULIG_WORKER_REPOS=--repo /var/lib/bulig/repos/sandbox=/var/lib/bulig-worker/work/sandbox
